    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 220</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_220/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 01 May 2025 01:10:27 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_220/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;How should parts A and B in the code below be modified so that it compiles successfully?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#xA;&#x9;var m map[string]int        //A&#xA;&#x9;m[&amp;#34;a&amp;#34;] = 1 &#xA;&#x9;if v := m[&amp;#34;b&amp;#34;]; v != nil {  //B&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;fmt.Println(v)&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#xA;&#x9;m := make(map[string]int)&#xA;&#x9;m[&amp;#34;a&amp;#34;] = 1&#xA;&#x9;if v,ok := m[&amp;#34;b&amp;#34;]; ok {&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;fmt.Println(v)&#xA;&#x9;}&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Solution Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;At A, only the map m is declared without allocating memory space, so it cannot be assigned directly. You need to use make(). It is recommended to initialize a map directly using make() or a composite literal.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 157</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_157/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 10 Jan 2025 12:46:04 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_157/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;How should A and B in the following code be modified to compile successfully?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#xA;    var m map[string]int        //A&#xA;    m[&amp;#34;a&amp;#34;] = 1&#xA;    if v := m[&amp;#34;b&amp;#34;]; v != nil {  //B&#xA;        fmt.Println(v)&#xA;    }&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;// A&#xA;At point A, &lt;code&gt;map m&lt;/code&gt; is only declared, and no memory space is allocated. Writing to an uninitialized map will cause a panic.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Therefore, &lt;code&gt;var m map[string]int&lt;/code&gt; needs to be changed to &lt;code&gt;m := make(map[string]int)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 142</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_142/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Dec 2024 00:24:33 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_142/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;       var s map[string]int&#xA;       delete(s, &amp;#34;h&amp;#34;)&#xA;       fmt.Println(s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;])&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A. runtime panic&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B. 0&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;B&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/rfK0pIKBRRx&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;delete&lt;/code&gt; on an uninitialized map (not made with &lt;code&gt;make&lt;/code&gt;) will not cause an error.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Accessing an uninitialized map returns the zero value corresponding to the value type.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;extension&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Extension&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#extension&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Assigning to an uninitialized map will cause a panic.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
